        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87750369?u=ccc1f52005708ae16bcb50e325e02145bff0ef7d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/releases/tag/v8.0.12\">BCD release v8.0.12</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">/cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/pepelsbey/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/pepelsbey\">@pepelsbey</a> <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/wbamberg/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/wbamberg\">@wbamberg</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45336",
            "title": "Synchronize with BCD v8.0.12",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T01:16:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T01:14:53.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "OnkarRuikar",
                "url": "https://github.com/OnkarRuikar"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Seven small prose typos across six files:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">HighlightRegistry.highlightsFromPoint()</code> in the Firefox 150 release notes: \"providing <strong>an</strong> mechanism\" → \"a mechanism\".</li>\n<li>Scroll-driven animations timeline range names: \"a specific portion of <strong>an</strong> named animation timeline range\" → \"a named\".</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">listitem</code> role: \"must have one or more elements with the role <code class=\"notranslate\">listitem</code> as children, <strong>a</strong> one or more elements with the role of <code class=\"notranslate\">group</code>\" → \"<strong>or</strong> one or more elements\".</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">listitem</code> role: \"their own place in <strong>a pages</strong> table of contents\" → \"a page's\".</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">VTTCue()</code>: \"visible from 50 seconds to <strong>a one minute</strong>, five and a half seconds\" → \"to one minute\".</li>\n<li>Uploading files to a web server: \"a dash followed by <strong>a one or more letters</strong>\" → \"followed by one or more letters\".</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">flex-line-count</code>: a missing space in \"a <code class=\"notranslate\">flex-direction</code> value of <code class=\"notranslate\">`column`and</code>\", which renders as \"of columnand a\".</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These are straightforward mistakes rather than style preferences, and none are catchable by the existing lint rules.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">listitem</code> fix restores the meaning given in the ARIA specification, which defines the containment as \"one or more elements with role listitem as children, <strong>or</strong> one or more elements with role group that have one or more elements with role listitem as children\" — a list holds list items, or groups that hold list items. As written, the sentence has no verb connecting the two alternatives.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45335",
            "title": "Fix typos in prose",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T00:26:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T00:24:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Replaces three more British spellings with their American equivalents across 18 files: <code class=\"notranslate\">signalling</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">signaling</code> (11), <code class=\"notranslate\">labelled</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">labeled</code> (10), and one <code class=\"notranslate\">colour</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">color</code> on <code class=\"notranslate\">console.timeStamp()</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The writing style guide requires American English spelling: \"Use American-English spelling. […] Do not use variant spelling.\" <code class=\"notranslate\">npm run lint:typos</code> cannot catch these, because all three are valid dictionary words.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">signalling</code> is also inconsistent with the surrounding docs: the WebRTC guide it appears in is itself titled \"Signaling and video calling\" and lives at <code class=\"notranslate\">/Web/API/WebRTC_API/Signaling_and_video_calling</code>, and the WebRTC specification uses \"signaling\" throughout.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Occurrences that must keep the British spelling are deliberately untouched:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">aria-labelledby</code> and the prose describing it, including the note on the <code class=\"notranslate\">listbox</code> role page that \"labelled\", with two L's, is the correct spelling based on the accessibility API conventions.</li>\n<li>The verbatim Firefox error strings on <code class=\"notranslate\">SyntaxError: functions cannot be labelled</code> and the <code class=\"notranslate\">label</code> statement page.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">menu-labelled-open</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">favourite-colour</code> example repository names, and the <code class=\"notranslate\">colour</code> keys in the WebExtensions storage examples that mirror them.</li>\n<li>The style guide's own \"Incorrect:\" examples.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45334",
            "title": "Use American English spelling for signalling, labelled, and colour",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T00:23:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T00:22:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Replaces three British spellings with their American equivalents across 25 files: <code class=\"notranslate\">amongst</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">among</code> (12), <code class=\"notranslate\">learnt</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">learned</code> (13), <code class=\"notranslate\">spelt</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">spelled</code> (1).</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The writing style guide requires American English spelling: \"Use American-English spelling. […] Do not use variant spelling.\" All three words are listed at Dictionary.com as chiefly British variants of the American forms shown above.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">npm run lint:typos</code> cannot catch these, because they are valid dictionary words in their own right.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Every occurrence changed is running prose. None fell into the categories that must keep a British spelling — code identifiers, verbatim browser error strings, example repository names, or the style guide's own \"Incorrect:\" examples. After this change the repo has no remaining case-insensitive match for any of the three words.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45333",
            "title": "Use American English spelling for amongst, learnt, and spelt",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T00:19:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T00:18:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
